From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 08:30:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 026/105] w8a16 gemv: per-shape tuned tiles + in-launch fixup
 split-K (no extra launch)

[K,N]-contiguous fp8 weights now use wide-N tiles fed to tl.dot without a
transpose, and the small-N shapes (shared-expert gate_up/down, out_proj,
o_proj) use split-K with a counter-based fixup epilogue (the last CTA per
n-block reduces the fp32 partials and writes bf16; counters self-reset, so
CUDA-graph replay is safe; single per-device scratch => one stream only).
In-server W16: w8a16 family 6.99 -> 5.81 ms/step (shared_down 7 -> 4.1us,
gate_up 7.9 -> 6.6, out_proj 14 -> 13.1, in_proj_ba 9.4 -> 7.8); the draft
head and lm_head keep their original narrow configs (wide tiles were slower
for them in the server). Implemented by an Opus subagent from in-server
per-shape medians; two shapes pinned by the supervisor after profiling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
